      "message": "Documenting a suggestion for a possible follow up since it will actually be a behavior change. So we should land this CL first then consider the following follow on change.\n\nNow that we\u0027ve moved everything into a single SkPicture class, the indices store on DrawDrawable directly map 1:1 with the indices into fDrawablePicts. Thus we can actually safely recurse of those too to get amore accurate count of ops. To do that we\u0027d add the following override here:\n```\n    void operator()(const SkRecords::DrawDrawable\u0026 op) {\n        if (fDrawablePicts \u0026\u0026 op.index \u003e\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026 op.index \u003c fDrawablePicts-\u003ecount()) {\n            fCount +\u003d fDrawablePicts-\u003ebegin()[op.index]-\u003eapproximateOpCount(true);\n        } else {\n            fCount +\u003d 1;\n        }\n    }\n```\n\nWe\u0027d also need to store `const SkSnapshotArray* fDrawablePicts;` on this class and initialize it approximateOpCount with: `NestedApproxOpCounter visitor(fDrawablePicts.get());`",
